    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the rule that rejects creating an owner when the owner's city already contains 50 or more owners, responding with **409 Conflict**.\n\nChanges, following the existing Spring conventions in this codebase (the same pattern used by `DuplicateTelephoneException`/`DuplicateOwnerException`):\n\n1. **New exception** `rest/advice/OwnerCityFullException.java` \u2014 a `RuntimeException` signalling the city-capacity violation.\n\n2. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler(OwnerCityFullException.class)` that returns a `409 Conflict` `ProblemDetail` reporting the `city` field, mirroring the other business-rule handlers.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1`** \u2014 added a `MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY = 50` constant and a `requireCityHasCapacity(city)` check wired into the existing `normalizeAndValidate(...)` pipeline used by `addOwner`. It counts existing owners whose city matches case-insensitively (consistent with how `generateCustomerCode` compares cities) and throws when the count is \u2265 50.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` (fills a fresh city to exactly 50, expects the 51st to be rejected) passes, and the full suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
